    <!--
      Item 16's per-conversation switch, drawn in the composer's own area because that is where the
      hold it governs is reported. It is on for a room the owner has never touched: a doubtful
      translation - one no reader could vouch for, or an answer in the wrong language - is held for
      the owner's tap rather than sent. It is deliberately not a setting on the settings screen: the
      exception is per room, and a global switch would leave the bug in every room it was not used on.
    -->
    <string name="tulkki_doubt_hold">Hold doubtful translations</string>
    <!--
      The same switch's visible word when it is the small chip in the composer's input row rather than
      the full-width labelled row it replaced (the owner: the label beside a full-size switch was
      "really in-your-face"). The full sentence above is the chip's accessible name, so the setting is
      still named for a screen reader; the chip's short word keeps the row quiet.
    -->
    <string name="tulkki_doubt_hold_chip">Doubtful</string>
    <!--
      The two doubt kinds' own sentences, and the two buttons the composer's bar offers for them
      (docs/MIGRATION.md item 16). "Tap to send it" was one sentence for both, and it was false for the
      echo: the answer is the owner's own words, so the tap re-asks rather than sending. The other
      kind - an answer no reader could vouch for - is a real translation, so its button sends the
      stored answer as it stands. The action lives on the bar because the bar is always visible and
      already has a button slot; the bubble's tap is installed per row by a verdict recomputed when
      the row is bound, so a row whose verdict no longer holds has no listener to tap.
    -->
    <string name="tulkki_hold_doubt_echo">Not sent: the translation came back unchanged, so nothing was translated.</string>
    <string name="tulkki_hold_doubt_send">Send it</string>
    <!--
      A send failure - the retry was tried and did not send - offers two actions on the bar: the retry
      (whose wording is the owner-editable setting below) and this one, the owner's one exception to
      "nothing is sent untranslated". It is per message, never automatic and never a setting.
    -->
    <string name="tulkki_hold_send_as_written">Send as written</string>
    <!--
      The held send's retry action is UI copy the owner may rewrite. It is a settings row of its own,
      down with the sent-side behaviour and never behind the prompts container, because it is not an
